      ":question/id": "6fa02f8c-3cdc-53b5-a8d2-e3b597f6470e",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ (\\sqrt{y})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- \\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\sqrt{y})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- \\sqrt{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sqrt{y})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (- \\sqrt{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sqrt{y})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- \\sqrt{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2 y^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3} & =- \\frac{2 x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}+K \\\\ y^{\\frac{3}{2}} & =- x^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3}{2}K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\ny^{\\frac{3}{2}}=- x^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C.\n$$",
