      ":question/id": "cd4d8278-9c71-5774-9d4e-c34413292177",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}}{x \\tan{\\left(y \\right)}}.$ for $x\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Also require $y\\ne 0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2 \\cos{\\left(y \\right)}}{x \\tan{\\left(y \\right)}} \\\\ (\\tan{\\left(y \\right)} \\sec{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\tan{\\left(y \\right)} \\sec{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\tan{\\left(y \\right)} \\sec{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\tan{\\left(y \\right)} \\sec{\\left(y \\right)})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\sec{\\left(y \\right)} & =2 \\ln{\\left(\\left|{x}\\right| \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\sec{\\left(y \\right)}=2 \\ln{\\left(\\left|{x}\\right| \\right)}+C.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
